//? Title: Piecewise linear interpolation
//? Subtitle: Actual interval searches, original sine grids and explicit extrapolation
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Joining neighboring samples gives a simple continuous interpolant with local
smooth-function error of second order. We inspect the actual selected interval
and blend, retain the original seven-node sine figure and six-row refinement
study, and distinguish interior interpolation from unbounded end-segment
extrapolation. An owned native interpolator validates knots once for repeated
queries; the legacy scalar API now checks every complete borrowed input.
)

\toc

> The local line and its remainder

For selected endpoints(x_k,y_k),(x_{k+1},y_{k+1}), the line is

$$t=\frac{x-x_k}{x_{k+1}-x_k},\qquad L(x)=y_k+t(y_{k+1}-y_k).$$
\alttext(The actual fractional position between selected neighboring abscissae blends their ordinates along one straight line.)

Inside the segment,0<=t<=1 gives a convex blend. Adjacent lines agree at knots,
hence continuity, though slopes can jump. For a
twice-continuously-differentiable underlying function sampled exactly, the
degree1 remainder is f''(xi)*(x−x_k)*(x−x_{k+1})/2 on that local interval, so
its magnitude is at most h_k^2*max|f''|/8. This is an exact-arithmetic
smooth-function statement, not an unconditional floating-point enclosure, an
error rate for arbitrary nonsmooth data or a bound on exterior extrapolation.
Affine functions have zero mathematical interpolation error.

> An actual bracket and blend

Retain the original affine nodes0,1,3,6 and values1,4,10,19 from y=3*x+1. At
query2.5, the actual selected interval is[1,3], t=0.75 and value8.5. Native
trace records the real endpoint guards and upper-bound mid comparisons; the
report never rebuilds a binary-search history.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/linear_interp_bracket.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const dm::algorithms::LinearInterpolator f({0, 1, 3, 6}, {1, 4, 10, 19});
    auto t = f.trace(2.5);
    auto &e = t.evaluation;
    std::print("| actual probe role (0:first,1:penultimate,2:mid) | actual knot index | actual knot x " "| actual predicate |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto &p : t.probes)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", p.kind, p.knot, p.abscissa,
                   p.predicate);
    std::print("\nActual selected interval {}; endpoints({},{}),({},{}); actual t {}; actual value {}.\n",
               e.interval, e.left_x, e.left_y, e.right_x, e.right_y, e.fraction,
               e.value);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("left", {0, 2},
           std::format("Actual selected left\n({}, {})", e.left_x, e.left_y)).node("right", {0, -2}, std::format("Actual selected right\n({}, {})", e.right_x, e.right_y)).node("blend", {7, 0}, std::format("Actual query{}; t{}\nvalue{}", e.query, e.fraction, e.value)).edge("left", "blend").edge("right", "blend").save_svg("build/linear_interp_bracket.svg");
}
```
