> Original refinement table and smooth second-order behavior

Retain node counts3,5,9,17,33,65 and the original1001-point error grid. Observed
maxima range only over that finite grid; they are not claimed continuous
suprema. For sine, max|f|<=1 gives the h^2/8 mathematical reference. Pairwise
observed orders are printed with a first-row sentinel0. The plots use actual
errors and the labelled theoretical reference, avoiding the claim that every
finite coarse refinement must quarter a rounded grid maximum exactly.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/linear_interp_refinement.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y, reference;
    double previous = 0;
    std::print("| original nodes | actual prescribed h | actual1001-grid maximum error | smooth " "h-squared-over8 reference | observed pairwise order, first row0 sentinel |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {3, 5, 9, 17, 33, 65}) {
        auto s = dm::algorithms::linear_interpolation_sine_study(n, 1000);
        std::print("| {} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} | {:.8f} |\n", n,
                   s.spacing, s.max_grid_error, s.error_reference,
                   previous ? std::log2(previous / s.max_grid_error) : 0);
        previous = s.max_grid_error;
        x.push_back(std::log2(s.spacing));
        y.push_back(std::log2(s.max_grid_error));
        reference.push_back(std::log2(s.error_reference));
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, reference, "smooth theory reference", {22, 163, 74}, 1.5).line(
        x, y, "actual grid errors", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, y, "",
                                                             {37, 99, 235}, 5).title("Original refinement controls and smooth error reference").x_label("log2(prescribed node spacing)").y_label("log2(error or reference)").save_svg("build/linear_interp_refinement.svg");
}
```
