> Exterior values extrapolate, and finite arithmetic still has limits

With nodes0,1,3 and values0,2,3, exterior queries−1 and4 evaluate the first and
last segment lines, giving−2 and3.5. Their fractions lie outside[0,1], so the
interior convex-range interpretation no longer applies. Knots are returned
exactly as stored. Complete data/order/query guards prevent empty, ragged,
duplicate, descending or nonfinite lookup inputs.

The fallback preserves some finite results when ordinary differences overflow:
for abscissae−DBL_MAX,+DBL_MAX and values1,3, query0 produces2 via widened
arithmetic. That is not a promise that all finite exterior inputs have
representable outputs; produced out-of-range values still throw. It also cannot
recover information already lost when a caller rounded its input coordinates.

The figure shows actual end-segment continuation and actual interior values on
one native interpolator, with original nodes retained.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/linear_interp_extrapolation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const dm::algorithms::LinearInterpolator f({0, 1, 3}, {0, 2, 3});
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual query | actual selected interval | actual fraction | actual value | actual " "exterior flag | actual numeric-node flag |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (double q : {-1., 0., .5, 1., 2., 3., 4.}) {
        auto e = f.evaluate(q);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", q, e.interval,
                   e.fraction, e.value, e.extrapolated, e.exact_node);
        x.push_back(q);
        y.push_back(e.value);
    }
    const double m = std::numeric_limits<double>::max();
    const dm::algorithms::LinearInterpolator wide({-m, m}, {1, 3});
    auto e = wide.evaluate(0);
    std::print("\nActual extreme-knot midpoint {}; actual widened fallback {}.\n",
               e.value, e.widened);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual line evaluations", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(
        x, y, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4).points(f.xs(), f.ys(), "original nodes",
                                           {220, 38, 38}, 7).y_limits(-3, 5.5).title("Actual exterior queries continue the end-segment lines").x_label("actual query x").y_label("actual interpolated or extrapolated value").save_svg("build/linear_interp_extrapolation.svg");
}
```
