> Contracts and verification

The legacy scalar function fully validates borrowed knots on every call, so its
total query time includes O(n) validation. The new owned interpolator
validates/copies once, then uses O(log n) interval selection and O(1) ordinary
query storage without rescanning all knots. Both share the same producing
search/blend and preserve the ordinary finite y0+t*(y1−y0) operation order.
Numeric endpoint matches use the actual stored ordinate directly; nonfinite
ordinary intermediates trigger a checked widened line evaluation. No input
mutation, hidden clamping or shared state is introduced.

Optional trace conservatively admits2*n+2+bit_width(n) logical input/probe
records before copying/evaluation; actual captured_entries is2*n plus the real
number of segment-selection comparisons and can be smaller. Default cap is one
million,0 disables only that optional cap, and fields/capacities/result/runtime
copies and bytes/RAM are excluded. Full knots and every actual probe are owned;
validation and blend-branch checks are explicitly outside the selected
search-probe counters.

Native tests compare 12100 queries with independent widened line evaluations and
check actual bracket probes, exact nodes, original sine grids, extrapolation,
finite-range fallbacks, quotas and ownership. The ten-report batch passed 101
native CTest cases, 34 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases, 103
compiled/executed public examples, 515/515 scoped file definitions plus 10 exact
LCG class definitions, and ten representative clangd hovers. Independent Python
integer/Fraction, explicit-label graph search, quadratic sequence DP and full
weighted-stump references passed 69430 records across all ten topics, including
a separately fitted held-out Iris model. Frozen ordinary compatibility passed
1000 Lex-BFS orders, 1000 library sorts, 100 LBG codebooks, 100 complete
five-round LogitBoost ensembles and 200 LLL bases; corrected LBG final
labels/objectives are intentionally excluded from historical compatibility. All
4 complete programs executed and all 4 native figures were rendered and visually
reviewed, with clipped legends corrected and rerun. HTML/Markdown
computed-result and figure-byte checks gate legacy retirement. Repeatable
receipts are retained in `build/mepml-conversion/batch-204-213/`.

> References

NIST,
[Digital Library of Mathematical Functions,§3.3 Interpolation|https://dlmf.nist.gov/3.3].
The local degree1 remainder gives the interior smooth-function reference; this
report distinguishes it from finite-grid observations, floating-point arithmetic
and exterior extrapolation.
